# Root ignores for the Senthra project.
# Per-project rules live in backend/.gitignore and frontend/.gitignore.

# Dependencies (defensive — should not exist at the root)
node_modules/

# OS junk (patterns without a slash apply to every subfolder)
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
ehthumbs.db
Desktop.ini

# Editor / IDE
.idea/
.vscode/
*.swp
*~

# Qodo AI workspace (local, regenerated)
.qodo/

# Claude Code — per-machine local config, never tracked anywhere in the tree.
.claude/

# Agent instruction files and the whole docs/ folder: LOCAL ONLY, never pushed.
# They stay on disk and keep working for the tooling that reads them — they are
# untracked (git rm --cached), not deleted.
#
# docs/ is ignored WHOLESALE rather than by file type, so nothing new dropped in
# there can leak: it holds internal design specs, client contract inputs (.docx,
# .pdf), real job-pack spreadsheets and the architecture diagrams. Its client
# inputs are commercial documents, and the diagrams describe internal flows —
# none of it is anyone's deliverable.
#
# What the reader of this repo gets instead: PROJECT-DOCUMENTATION.md and the
# per-app READMEs, which stay tracked.
#
# NOTE for anyone switching branches: these files exist as ignored-and-untracked
# only on branches where the removal commit is present. Checking out a branch
# from BEFORE that commit restores them as tracked files, and moving forward
# again deletes them off disk. Keep a copy outside the repo.
/CLAUDE.md
/frontend/CLAUDE.md
/frontend/AGENTS.md
/mobile/CLAUDE.md
/mobile/AGENTS.md
/docs/

# Logs
*.log

# Frozen UI reference snapshot — local only.
# A read-only copy of the starter dashboard's demo screens (see reference/README.md).
# It is outside frontend/ and backend/, so nothing type-checks, lints, bundles or imports
# it — only a handful of code comments point at it by name. Untracked so it stops riding
# along in every clone and diff. Earlier revisions remain in git history, so the snapshot
# is still recoverable with `git show <commit>:reference/<file>`.
reference/

# Binary client / reference docs — keep the .md summaries tracked, ignore the
# source binaries (PDFs, Word, Excel: client inputs, job packs, samples, etc.)
*.pdf
*.docx
*.doc
*.xlsx
*.xls
*.pptx
*.ppt

# Safety net: never commit real secrets anywhere in the tree.
# (.env.example templates are still allowed.)
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
